<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
I worked on leveling Leat a little this weekend.  I spent about 5 hours and got half way to 52 quad kiting Spirocs in the Timorous Deep.  They are good experience, have a high spawn rate and are in a very concentrated area.  This makes them ideal for gaining lots of experience in a short period of time.  (The only downfall is that you can not bind in that zone so making runs to the store/bank is time consuming.)<P>Now with the new announcement I am giving second thoughts to leveling Leat.  When I first heard about the new bonuses they mentioned characters that had maxed out their experience at level 60.  They could trade in a Yellow bubble for some stats enhancement.  Now it looks as if anyone level 51 or higher will be able to use this feature.  I&#8217;m all for this by the way.<P>My thought is that it is much easier for me to find experience bearing mobs at level 51 than it will be for me to find them at level 52 let alone level 60.  I know that most of the Spirocs will go green on me at level 52 and I will have to go hunt in some other zone like the hugely overcrowded CS zone.<P>I'm thinking that if I want to take advantage of this Stats Enhancement toggle it would be wise for me to wait for the SOL expansion.<P>Any thoughts?
</FONT>
